/* 
SPACE COMMIES - SNL Sketch
Runtime: 3:30 (210 seconds)
Format: Single-camera sketch
Tone: Deadpan patriotic absurdism

LOGLINE: On a forgettable Starfleet vessel, a Captain decides to space 
some communist prisoners. Her First Officer objects on procedural grounds, 
but the Captain's logic is so sound that he eventually agrees spacing 
commies is just good policy.

CAST:
- THE CAPTAIN (Host or strong featured player) - Deadpan authoritarian
- FIRST OFFICER (Strong straight man) - Voice of reason who breaks
- ENGINEER (High energy) - Enthusiastic enabler
- ENSIGN (Young cast member) - Cheerful complicity
- ADMIRAL (Cameo/viewscreen) - Authority figure

SET: Generic Starfleet bridge - NOT the Enterprise. This is USS [REDACTED], 
one of those forgettable ships where terrible things happen off-screen.
*/

INT. STARFLEET BRIDGE - CONTINUOUS

Red alert lights FLASH. Klaxon BLARES softly in background.

THE CAPTAIN sits in the command chair, center stage. FIRST OFFICER stands beside her. ENGINEER at tactical station. ENSIGN at operations console.

Generic sci-fi bridge - deliberately forgettable. Visible airlock door stage left.

> COLD OPEN (0:00-0:30) <

FIRST OFFICER
Captain, we've apprehended the Space Communists who were redistributing replicator rations.

CAPTAIN
(calm, measured)
Excellent. Prepare to jettison them out the airlock.

FIRST OFFICER
(concerned)
Captain, Starfleet regulations require we beam them to a rehabilitation colony.

CAPTAIN
(deadpan)
I'm not going to follow Starfleet regulations.

FIRST OFFICER
(shocked)
That's... that's murder.

CAPTAIN
I'm not going to follow morality.

ENGINEER jumps up from station, WAY too excited.

ENGINEER
(enthusiastic)
I'll get the airlock ready!

ENSIGN
(cheerful, turning to Captain)
Depressurization sequence standing by, Captain!

> THE ESCALATION (0:30-2:00) <

FIRST OFFICER
(desperate)
Captain, this violates the Prime Directive!

CAPTAIN
I'm not going to follow the Prime Directive.

FIRST OFFICER
The Geneva Convention!

CAPTAIN
I'm not going to follow the Geneva Convention.

FIRST OFFICER
(rapid-fire)
The Khitomer Accords! The Treaty of Algeron!

CAPTAIN
Nope. Not following those either.

FIRST OFFICER
(increasingly desperate)
Captain, you can't just ignore the laws of physics!

CAPTAIN
I'm not going to follow the laws of physics.

ENGINEER
(helpfully)
Actually, Captain, the laws of physics will help us space them faster.

CAPTAIN
(slight smile)
See? Physics is on my side.

FIRST OFFICER
(grasping at straws)
This goes against the laws of God!

CAPTAIN
I'm not going to follow the laws of God.

FIRST OFFICER
(frantic)
The laws of man! The laws of logic!

CAPTAIN
(dismissive wave)
Especially not logic.

ENSIGN
(cheerfully interrupting)
Captain, the communists are asking if they can at least have a trial.

CAPTAIN
I'm not going to follow due process.

> THE TWISTED LOGIC (1:20-2:00) <

FIRST OFFICER
(breaking down)
Captain, WHY are you doing this?

CAPTAIN
(calm, measured, reasonable tone)
Commander, if we beam them to a planet, they'll simply take over that planet. Then they'll use it as a base to spread their ideology. Before you know it, they've conquered the entire galaxy.
(beat)
But if we jettison them into space... the problem is solved. Permanently.

FIRST OFFICER processes this slowly. His resistance is crumbling.

FIRST OFFICER
(slowly)
That's... that's...

ENGINEER
(excited)
Brilliant!

ENSIGN
(nodding)
So efficient!

FIRST OFFICER
(slowly, reluctantly)
Captain... I hate to say this, but... I see your point.

CAPTAIN
(gracious)
Thank you, Commander.

FIRST OFFICER
(converted)
If we show mercy, we're just enabling future conquest.

CAPTAIN
Exactly. The needs of the many outweigh the needs of the few.

> THE BUTTON (2:00-3:30) <

ENSIGN
Captain, incoming transmission from Starfleet Command.

CAPTAIN
On screen.

The VIEWSCREEN ACTIVATES with a brief electronic BEEP.

ADMIRAL appears on viewscreen - stern, authoritative.

ADMIRAL
Captain of the [REDACTED], we've received reports you're about to space some prisoners.

CAPTAIN
That's correct, Admiral.

ADMIRAL
(authoritative)
That's a clear violation of—

CAPTAIN
(interrupting)
I'm not going to follow Starfleet Command.

ADMIRAL
(angry)
Captain, I'm ORDERING you to—

CAPTAIN
I'm not going to follow orders.

CAPTAIN gestures to ENSIGN. ENSIGN presses button.

Transmission CUTS. Viewscreen goes DARK.

ENGINEER
(at airlock controls)
Airlock ready, Captain!

CAPTAIN
(simple nod)
Proceed.

SOUND EFFECT: Airlock opening - WHOOSH of decompression.

Beat of silence. The crew looks satisfied. Red alert lights continue flashing.

ENSIGN
(checking console)
Captain, we're receiving a distress call from a nearby ship. They say they're being attacked by... Space Fascists.

CAPTAIN
(immediate, compassionate)
Beam them aboard immediately. We'll give them sanctuary.

FIRST OFFICER
(confused)
Captain, isn't that hypocritical?

CAPTAIN
(deadpan, final line)
I'm not going to follow consistency.

BLACKOUT.

FADE OUT.

THE END

